new file mode 100644
index 0000000..47ac86d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-airoha-pon-mac
@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/airoha-pon-mac/<dev>/serial_number
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.18
+Contact:	mmmorks <john@morkel.me>
+Description:
+		(RW) The ONU serial number the MAC presents to the OLT
+		(ITU-T G.984.3, G.9807.1): the vendor ID as four printable
+		characters followed by the vendor-specific part as eight hex
+		digits, for example ABCD0123abcd. Reads empty until set. The
+		MAC does not start without one. Writable only while the MAC is
+		stopped.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/airoha-pon-mac/<dev>/password
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.18
+Contact:	mmmorks <john@morkel.me>
+Description:
+		(WO) The 10-byte ONU password of GPON (ITU-T G.984.3): 20 hex
+		digits, or up to 10 characters taken as they are and padded
+		with zero bytes. All zero bytes until written. Writable only
+		while the MAC is stopped.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/airoha-pon-mac/<dev>/registration_id
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.18
+Contact:	mmmorks <john@morkel.me>
+Description:
+		(WO) The 36-byte registration ID of XGS-PON (ITU-T G.9807.1):
+		72 hex digits, or up to 36 characters taken as they are and
+		padded with zero bytes. All zero bytes until written. Writable
+		only while the MAC is stopped.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/airoha-pon-mac/<dev>/master_session_key
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.18
+Contact:	mmmorks <john@morkel.me>
+Description:
+		(WO) The 16-byte master session key of XGS-PON (ITU-T
+		G.9807.1), as 32 hex digits: the key the OMCI layer has once
+		the OLT authenticated the ONU through enhanced security
+		control (ITU-T G.988 9.13.11). The MAC derives the OMCI and
+		PLOAM integrity keys and the key encryption key from it into
+		the key set not in use. OMCI moves to its new key at once;
+		PLOAM and the key encryption key at the OLT's next Request
+		Registration. Writing the key set already is a no-op.
+
+		The key lasts until the next activation, which derives the
+		default keys again; write it again after a new
+		authentication. Writable only on a running XGS-PON line once
+		its keys are derived: -ENETDOWN when the MAC is stopped,
+		-EOPNOTSUPP on a GPON line, -EAGAIN before the keys are
+		derived, -EIO when a derivation did not finish.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/airoha-pon-mac/<dev>/line_mode
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.18
+Contact:	mmmorks <john@morkel.me>
+Description:
+		(RW) The line mode the next start runs: "auto", "gpon" or
+		"xgs-pon". A read lists all three with the configured one in
+		brackets. "auto", the default, needs the board's optics lines
+		and picks the mode of the optic that sees light; it takes about
+		six seconds. When neither does it picks XGS-PON. A pick made
+		with no light is tested again every 30 seconds until the PON
+		PHY sees light, each test stopping and starting the MAC. A line
+		that saw light, then lost its link for 30 seconds with no light
+		on its optic, is tested the same way: a fibre moved to the
+		other mode's OLT is followed, and while neither optic sees
+		light the line is kept. Writable only while the MAC is stopped.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/airoha-pon-mac/<dev>/line
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.18
+Contact:	mmmorks <john@morkel.me>
+Description:
+		(RO) The line mode the MAC runs in: "gpon", "xgs-pon", or
+		"none" while it is stopped.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/airoha-pon-mac/<dev>/enable
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.18
+Contact:	mmmorks <john@morkel.me>
+Description:
+		(RW) Write 1 to start the MAC and 0 to stop it. A start picks
+		the line mode, powers that mode's optic, brings up the PON PHY
+		and leaves the MAC in state O1. The MAC then runs the
+		activation by itself, towards O5: ITU-T G.984.3 in GPON,
+		ITU-T G.9807.1 in XGS-PON. A stop turns
+		the PHY and both optics off. Reads 1 while the MAC runs.
+		A power failure the board announces stops the MAC as a
+		write of 0 would, after its Dying Gasp; the attribute then
+		reads 0 and is notified.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/airoha-pon-mac/<dev>/state
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.18
+Contact:	mmmorks <john@morkel.me>
+Description:
+		(RO) The ONU activation state the running MAC holds: O1 to O7
+		(ITU-T G.984.3), or O1, O2-3 and O4 to O7 in XGS-PON
+		(ITU-T G.9807.1). "none" while the MAC is stopped. It is
+		pollable: every state change notifies poll(2) readers.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/airoha-pon-mac/<dev>/onu_id
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.18
+Contact:	mmmorks <john@morkel.me>
+Description:
+		(RO) The ONU-ID the OLT assigned, in decimal, or "none" before
+		one is assigned and while the MAC is stopped. It is the MAC's
+		register: in XGS-PON, after an Assign ONU-ID with another
+		ONU-ID in O4 or O5 moves the ONU to O1, it still shows the old
+		one until the MAC stops or the next Assign ONU-ID.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/drivers/airoha-pon-mac/<dev>/link
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.18
+Contact:	mmmorks <john@morkel.me>
+Description:
+		(RO) The PON PHY's last downstream report since the start:
+		"ready" (synchronised, with light), "lost", or "none" before
+		the first one. Pollable: a change notifies poll(2) readers.
diff --git a/Documentation/netlink/specs/airoha-pon-mac.yaml b/Documentation/netlink/specs/airoha-pon-mac.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..60128eb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/netlink/specs/airoha-pon-mac.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,765 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: ((GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note) OR BSD-3-Clause)
+---
+name: airoha-pon-mac
+
+protocol: genetlink
+
+uapi-header: linux/airoha_pon_mac.h
+
+doc: >-
+  The datapath configuration of an Airoha EN7581 PON MAC, for the
+  userspace OMCI agent: the GEM ports and T-CONTs the OLT provisions
+  through OMCI (ITU-T G.988), the rules that put upstream frames on a
+  GEM port, and the activation state the OLT's PLOAM messages drive.
+  A device is named by the ifindex of its PON netdev. table-set
+  replaces all three tables at once, and changes nothing when it is
+  refused. The driver keeps the tables across a re-activation, and binds each
+  T-CONT entry and GEM port to the T-CONT the OLT's Alloc-ID currently
+  has, again whenever PLOAM assigns or withdraws one.
+
+definitions:
+  -
+    type: const
+    name: queues
+    value: 8
+    doc: Upstream queues of one T-CONT.
+  -
+    type: enum
+    name: line
+    doc: The line mode the MAC runs in.
+    entries:
+      -
+        name: none
+        doc: The MAC is stopped.
+      -
+        name: gpon
+        doc: ITU-T G.984.3.
+      -
+        name: xgs-pon
+        doc: ITU-T G.9807.1.
+  -
+    type: flags
+    name: direction
+    doc: The directions a GEM port carries.
+    entries:
+      -
+        name: upstream
+        doc: >-
+          Frames go up on the GEM port. It needs an Alloc-ID, and while
+          the OLT has not assigned that Alloc-ID they are dropped.
+      -
+        name: downstream
+        doc: Frames that arrive on the GEM port are delivered.
+  -
+    type: enum
+    name: key-ring
+    doc: >-
+      The encryption the OLT set for a GEM port, numbered as ITU-T G.988's
+      GEM port network CTP Encryption key ring.
+    entries:
+      -
+        name: none
+        doc: No encryption.
+      -
+        name: unicast
+        doc: Unicast encryption, both directions.
+      -
+        name: broadcast
+        doc: Broadcast (multicast) encryption, downstream only.
+      -
+        name: unicast-downstream
+        doc: Unicast encryption, downstream only.
+  -
+    type: enum
+    name: reboot-depth
+    doc: >-
+      What an XGS-PON Reboot_ONU asks for, numbered as its Reboot depth
+      (ITU-T G.9807.1 Table C.11.23A).
+    entries:
+      -
+        name: mib-reset
+        doc: A MIB reset (ITU-T G.988 clause 9.1.3), and no reboot.
+      -
+        name: omci-reboot
+        doc: The equivalent of an OMCI reboot (ITU-T G.988 clause A.2.35).
+      -
+        name: power-cycle
+        doc: The equivalent of a power cycle.
+      -
+        name: config-reset
+        doc: >-
+          Clear the configuration saved in non-volatile memory, then a MIB
+          reset and a reboot. The factory configuration, the registration
+          ID and the software images stay as they are.
+  -
+    type: enum
+    name: reboot-image
+    doc: >-
+      The software image a Reboot_ONU asks to run after the reboot, numbered
+      as its Reboot image. Ignored with the mib-reset depth.
+    entries:
+      -
+        name: committed
+        doc: The image that is committed.
+      -
+        name: uncommitted
+        doc: The image that is not committed.
+  -
+    type: enum
+    name: reboot-state
+    doc: >-
+      The activation states a Reboot_ONU applies in, numbered as its ONU
+      state octet.
+    entries:
+      -
+        name: any
+        doc: Any state.
+      -
+        name: o1-o2-3
+        doc: O1 and O2-3 only.
+  -
+    type: enum
+    name: reboot-calls
+    doc: >-
+      The voice call condition of a Reboot_ONU, numbered as bits 2-1 of its
+      Flags octet.
+    entries:
+      -
+        name: any
+        doc: Reboot whatever calls are in progress.
+      -
+        name: no-call
+        doc: Reboot only while no POTS or VoIP call is in progress.
+      -
+        name: no-emergency-call
+        doc: Reboot only while no emergency call is in progress.
+
+attribute-sets:
+  -
+    name: dev
+    attributes:
+      -
+        name: ifindex
+        type: u32
+        doc: The PON netdev.
+        checks:
+          min: 1
+      -
+        name: line
+        type: u32
+        enum: line
+        doc: The line mode the MAC runs in.
+      -
+        name: state
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The activation state the MAC is in, 1 to 7 for O1 to O7 in GPON.
+          In XGS-PON, 2 is O2-3 and 3 never appears. Absent while the MAC
+          is stopped.
+      -
+        name: onu-id
+        type: u32
+        doc: The ONU-ID the OLT assigned. Absent when it has assigned none.
+      -
+        name: omcc-port
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The GEM port of the OMCI channel, as the OLT configured it.
+          Absent while there is none.
+      -
+        name: tcont
+        type: nest
+        multi-attr: true
+        nested-attributes: tcont
+        doc: >-
+          A T-CONT. A dump lists every Alloc-ID the OLT assigned and every
+          configured one; table-set takes the configuration.
+      -
+        name: gem
+        type: nest
+        multi-attr: true
+        nested-attributes: gem
+        doc: A GEM port.
+      -
+        name: rule
+        type: nest
+        multi-attr: true
+        nested-attributes: rule
+        doc: An upstream classification rule, in match order.
+      -
+        name: check
+        type: flag
+        doc: >-
+          table-set only checks the tables and changes nothing: it fails
+          exactly where the same request without the flag would be refused.
+      -
+        name: fec
+        type: nest
+        nested-attributes: fec
+        doc: >-
+          The downstream FEC counters, cumulative since the device was
+          bound. They count only while the MAC runs.
+      -
+        name: ber
+        type: nest
+        nested-attributes: ber
+        doc: >-
+          The last BER interval's sample. Absent before the first one.
+      -
+        name: omci-ifindex
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The OMCI netdev: bare OMCI messages, one per frame, on the
+          OMCI channel's GEM port. It has its carrier while the line
+          has an OMCI channel, and drops it on every loss of one only
+          after the last message received on the lost channel was
+          delivered.
+      -
+        name: omci-integrity
+        type: flag
+        doc: >-
+          The driver owns the integrity trailer of the OMCI messages in
+          the current line mode: the CRC on a GPON line, the MIC under
+          the OMCI integrity key on an XGS-PON line. It delivers on the
+          OMCI netdev only the messages whose trailer was checked, with
+          the trailer removed, and adds the trailer to every message sent
+          there. The MAC checks and removes the trailer; an XGS-PON
+          message that arrives with its MIC has the MIC checked by the
+          driver, which drops it when it fails. Absent in a line mode
+          where it does not.
+      -
+        name: reboot
+        type: nest
+        nested-attributes: reboot
+        doc: An XGS-PON Reboot_ONU the OLT sent. reboot-ntf only.
+      -
+        name: xgs
+        type: nest
+        nested-attributes: xgs
+        doc: >-
+          The XGS-PON line counters ITU-T G.988's XG-PON TC and management
+          PM read, cumulative since the device was bound. Present while the
+          line is XGS-PON.
+  -
+    name: tcont
+    attributes:
+      -
+        name: alloc-id
+        type: u32
+        doc: The Alloc-ID that names the T-CONT.
+        checks:
+          max: 0x3fff
+      -
+        name: index
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The frame engine T-CONT that carries the Alloc-ID. Present only
+          while the OLT has assigned it.
+      -
+        name: strict
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          How many queues, from queue 7 down, are served by strict
+          priority: 0 to 8, but not 7. The other queues share what those
+          leave by weight.
+        checks:
+          max: queues
+      -
+        name: weight
+        type: u32
+        multi-attr: true
+        doc: >-
+          The weight of each queue, from queue 0 up: as many as the
+          T-CONT has queues, or none when all are strict.
+        checks:
+          max: 0xffff
+      -
+        name: rate
+        type: u32
+        doc: The upstream rate limit in kbit/s, 0 for none.
+      -
+        name: burst
+        type: u32
+        doc: The burst size of the rate limit, in bytes.
+      -
+        name: cpu-packets
+        type: u32
+        doc: Frames the CPU sent on the T-CONT. A free-running counter.
+      -
+        name: fwd-packets
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          Frames the flow offload forwarded to the T-CONT. A free-running
+          counter.
+  -
+    name: gem
+    attributes:
+      -
+        name: port-id
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The GEM Port-ID. A GPON line has 12-bit Port-IDs, so one above
+          0xfff never matches a frame there.
+        checks:
+          max: 0xfffe
+      -
+        name: direction
+        type: u32
+        enum: direction
+        enum-as-flags: true
+        doc: The directions the GEM port carries.
+      -
+        name: alloc-id
+        type: u32
+        doc: The Alloc-ID of the T-CONT that carries the upstream frames.
+        checks:
+          max: 0x3fff
+      -
+        name: encrypted
+        type: flag
+        doc: >-
+          The OLT encrypts the GEM port's downstream frames (PLOAM
+          Encrypted Port-ID). GPON only, reported only; an XGS-PON line
+          takes key-ring instead.
+      -
+        name: queue
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The queue of the T-CONT that carries the upstream frames, 0 to
+          7 with 7 the highest, as strict and weight number them. Absent
+          is queue 0.
+        checks:
+          max: 7
+      -
+        name: rx-frames
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          GEM frames received on the port. This and the three counters
+          after it are reported only, cumulative since the device was
+          bound: they count while the GPON MAC has the port open, except
+          from a change to its GEM ports until it rewrites its counter
+          index 2 s after the last one, and are 0 for a port it never
+          opened.
+      -
+        name: rx-payload-bytes
+        type: uint
+        doc: Payload bytes received on the port.
+      -
+        name: tx-frames
+        type: uint
+        doc: GEM frames transmitted on the port.
+      -
+        name: tx-payload-bytes
+        type: uint
+        doc: Payload bytes transmitted on the port.
+      -
+        name: ani-ifindex
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The ANI port device (an airoha-pon-ani link on the PON
+          interface) the GEM port's downstream frames are delivered on.
+          Absent, or 0, for the PON interface itself. While the device is
+          gone or down, those frames are dropped.
+        checks:
+          max: 0x7fffffff
+      -
+        name: key-ring
+        type: u32
+        enum: key-ring
+        doc: >-
+          The encryption the OLT set through OMCI (the port's GEM port
+          network CTP). On an XGS-PON line the MAC encrypts the port's
+          upstream frames when it is unicast; the downstream needs nothing
+          from the driver, as each XGEM frame header names its key. A GPON
+          line takes no notice, as there the OLT's PLOAM Encrypted Port-ID
+          decides. Absent is none.
+  -
+    name: rule
+    attributes:
+      -
+        name: vid
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The VLAN ID of the frame's outer tag. Absent, together with
+          untagged, to match any frame.
+        checks:
+          max: 4095
+      -
+        name: untagged
+        type: flag
+        doc: Match a frame without a VLAN tag; excludes vid.
+      -
+        name: pcp
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The priority of the frame's outer tag, 0 for a frame without
+          one. Absent to match any priority.
+        checks:
+          max: 7
+      -
+        name: port-id
+        type: u32
+        doc: The GEM port a matching frame goes up on.
+        checks:
+          max: 0xfffe
+      -
+        name: ani-ifindex
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The device whose frames the rule classifies: an ANI port device
+          (an airoha-pon-ani link on the PON interface), or, absent or 0,
+          the PON interface itself. A frame is tried against the rules of
+          the device it is sent on only.
+        checks:
+          max: 0x7fffffff
+
+  -
+    name: fec
+    attributes:
+      -
+        name: corrected-bytes
+        type: uint
+        doc: Bytes the FEC decoder corrected.
+      -
+        name: corrected-words
+        type: uint
+        doc: Codewords the FEC decoder corrected.
+      -
+        name: uncorrectable-words
+        type: uint
+        doc: Codewords the FEC decoder could not correct.
+      -
+        name: words
+        type: uint
+        doc: Codewords received.
+      -
+        name: errored-seconds
+        type: uint
+        doc: Seconds that saw a codeword the decoder could not correct.
+  -
+    name: ber
+    attributes:
+      -
+        name: sequence
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          The sample's number. It rises by one per BER interval and starts
+          at 1 when the device is bound.
+      -
+        name: errors
+        type: u32
+        doc: >-
+          The downstream errors of the interval. GPON: the BIP-8 errors its
+          frames carried. XGS-PON: the bytes the FEC decoder corrected,
+          plus 17 for each codeword it could not correct, a lower bound of
+          the bit errors.
+      -
+        name: interval
+        type: u32
+        doc: The interval, in milliseconds.
+      -
+        name: bits
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          The downstream bits the errors were counted over: XGS-PON only,
+          248 bytes for each codeword received. Absent on GPON, where the
+          errors are counted over the interval at the 2.48832 Gbit/s line
+          rate.
+  -
+    name: reboot
+    attributes:
+      -
+        name: depth
+        type: u32
+        enum: reboot-depth
+        doc: What the OLT asks for.
+      -
+        name: image
+        type: u32
+        enum: reboot-image
+        doc: The image to run after the reboot.
+      -
+        name: state-condition
+        type: u32
+        enum: reboot-state
+        doc: >-
+          The activation states the request applies in. The driver does not
+          check it; the dev state in the same message is the state the MAC
+          was in when the message arrived.
+      -
+        name: calls
+        type: u32
+        enum: reboot-calls
+        doc: >-
+          The voice call condition, as sent: 3 is reserved, and the driver
+          does not check it.
+      -
+        name: other-onu
+        type: flag
+        doc: >-
+          The message was broadcast and names another ONU's serial number,
+          so it is not for this ONU (ITU-T G.9807.1 inspects the serial
+          number of a broadcast one only, and one of zero addresses every
+          ONU). The driver still passes it on.
+
+  -
+    name: xgs
+    doc: >-
+      The XGS-PON line counters. The ones the MAC keeps (the header, XGEM,
+      byte and MIC error counts, rx-ploam and tx-ploam) count from each
+      downstream ready to the MAC's next stop and are added up at least once
+      a second. The driver keeps the rest. Its PLOAM message counts by type
+      take the messages broadcast or to this ONU whose MIC checked out.
+    attributes:
+      -
+        name: psbd-hec-errors
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          Header errors in the downstream physical synchronization block,
+          as the MAC counts them: the XGTC header errors among them.
+      -
+        name: xgtc-hec-errors
+        type: uint
+        doc: Downstream XGTC headers that had errors.
+      -
+        name: unknown-profiles
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          Upstream grants that named a burst profile the ONU does not
+          hold.
+      -
+        name: tx-xgem-frames
+        type: uint
+        doc: XGEM frames sent.
+      -
+        name: tx-xgem-fragments
+        type: uint
+        doc: XGEM frames sent that carried a fragment of a frame.
+      -
+        name: xgem-hec-lost-words
+        type: uint
+        doc: Downstream words lost to XGEM header errors.
+      -
+        name: xgem-key-errors
+        type: uint
+        doc: Downstream XGEM frames dropped because of their key.
+      -
+        name: xgem-hec-errors
+        type: uint
+        doc: Downstream XGEM headers that had errors.
+      -
+        name: tx-nonidle-bytes
+        type: uint
+        doc: Bytes of the non-idle XGEM frames sent.
+      -
+        name: rx-nonidle-bytes
+        type: uint
+        doc: Bytes of the non-idle XGEM frames received.
+      -
+        name: lods-events
+        type: uint
+        doc: Losses of downstream synchronization in O5.
+      -
+        name: lods-restored
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          Of those, the ones the downstream came back from before TO2
+          ran out.
+      -
+        name: lods-reactivations
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          Of those, the ones TO2 ran out on, so that the ONU activated
+          again.
+      -
+        name: rx-ploam-mic-errors
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          Downstream PLOAM messages whose MIC failed, as the MAC counts
+          them.
+      -
+        name: rx-ploam
+        type: uint
+        doc: Downstream PLOAM messages, as the MAC counts them.
+      -
+        name: rx-profile
+        type: uint
+        doc: Burst Profile messages received.
+      -
+        name: rx-ranging-time
+        type: uint
+        doc: Ranging Time messages received.
+      -
+        name: rx-deactivate-onu-id
+        type: uint
+        doc: Deactivate ONU-ID messages received.
+      -
+        name: rx-disable-serial-number
+        type: uint
+        doc: Disable Serial Number messages received.
+      -
+        name: rx-request-registration
+        type: uint
+        doc: Request Registration messages received.
+      -
+        name: rx-assign-alloc-id
+        type: uint
+        doc: Assign Alloc-ID messages received.
+      -
+        name: rx-key-control
+        type: uint
+        doc: Key Control messages received.
+      -
+        name: rx-sleep-allow
+        type: uint
+        doc: Sleep Allow messages received.
+      -
+        name: rx-omci-baseline
+        type: uint
+        doc: Baseline OMCI messages the OMCI netdev delivered.
+      -
+        name: rx-omci-extended
+        type: uint
+        doc: Extended OMCI messages the OMCI netdev delivered.
+      -
+        name: rx-assign-onu-id
+        type: uint
+        doc: Assign ONU-ID messages received.
+      -
+        name: rx-omci-mic-errors
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          Downstream OMCI messages whose MIC failed: the MAC's count,
+          and the messages that arrived with a MIC the driver checked
+          and dropped.
+      -
+        name: tx-ploam
+        type: uint
+        doc: Upstream PLOAM messages, as the MAC counts them.
+      -
+        name: tx-serial-number
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          Serial Number ONU messages the MAC sent. Two sent between two
+          runs of the interrupt handler count as one.
+      -
+        name: tx-registration
+        type: uint
+        doc: >-
+          Registration messages: the ones the MAC sent, counted as tx-
+          serial-number is, and the ones the driver sent.
+      -
+        name: tx-key-report
+        type: uint
+        doc: Key Report messages sent.
+      -
+        name: tx-acknowledge
+        type: uint
+        doc: Acknowledge messages sent.
+      -
+        name: tx-sleep-request
+        type: uint
+        doc: Sleep Request messages sent. The driver sends none.
+
+operations:
+  list:
+    -
+      name: dev-get
+      doc: >-
+        Get the activation state and the datapath tables of a device, or
+        dump every device.
+      attribute-set: dev
+      do:
+        pre: pmac-nl-pre-doit
+        post: pmac-nl-post-doit
+        request:
+          attributes:
+            - ifindex
+        reply: &dev-all
+          attributes:
+            - ifindex
+            - line
+            - state
+            - onu-id
+            - omcc-port
+            - tcont
+            - gem
+            - rule
+            - fec
+            - ber
+            - omci-ifindex
+            - omci-integrity
+            - xgs
+      dump:
+        pre: pmac-nl-pre-dumpit
+        reply: *dev-all
+    -
+      name: table-set
+      doc: >-
+        Replace the three datapath tables, each whole: an absent table is
+        an empty one. The T-CONT entries set the queue scheduling and rate
+        limit of each T-CONT, by Alloc-ID; a T-CONT without an entry keeps
+        the scheduling it has, and has no rate limit. The rules are tried
+        in order, the first match picking a frame's GEM port; a frame no
+        rule matches is dropped. A GEM port or rule naming an ifindex that
+        is not an ANI port device of the PON interface is refused. An ANI
+        port device removed later leaves the tables as they are: its GEM
+        ports' frames are dropped and its rules match nothing until a
+        table-set without it. With check, only the checks run.
+      attribute-set: dev
+      flags: [admin-perm]
+      do:
+        pre: pmac-nl-pre-doit
+        post: pmac-nl-post-doit
+        request:
+          attributes:
+            - ifindex
+            - tcont
+            - gem
+            - rule
+            - check
+    -
+      name: dev-change-ntf
+      doc: >-
+        The activation state, the ONU-ID, the OMCI channel or an Alloc-ID
+        changed. The GEM port counters in it are as last read, by a
+        dev-get or a change to the GEM ports, not read for it.
+      notify: dev-get
+      mcgrp: monitor
+    -
+      name: ber-ntf
+      doc: >-
+        A BER interval ended, which a line has only in O5: on GPON once the
+        OLT set an interval, the sample sent as the MAC reports the
+        interval's errors to the OLT; on XGS-PON every second, which has
+        no BER interval to report and sends no sample for an interval
+        that received no codeword.
+      attribute-set: dev
+      event:
+        attributes:
+          - ifindex
+          - ber
+      mcgrp: ber
+    -
+      name: reboot-ntf
+      doc: >-
+        The OLT sent an XGS-PON Reboot_ONU to this ONU-ID or broadcast,
+        with a MIC that passed and a depth, image and state condition in
+        range; the driver drops any other.
+        The driver reboots nothing and sends no reply; acting on it is the
+        listener's. A listener that missed it is not told
+        again.
+      attribute-set: dev
+      event:
+        attributes:
+          - ifindex
+          - state
+          - reboot
+      mcgrp: monitor
+
+mcast-groups:
+  list:
+    -
+      name: monitor
+    -
+      name: ber
